rustc_codegen_js: use safe Vec::push/reserve paths in non-trivial alloc::vec helpers.

`Vec::from_iter`, `Vec::extend` (`extend_desugared`, `extend_trusted`, and
`IntoIter` `SpecExtend`), non-`IsZero` `Vec::from_elem` / `Vec::extend_with`
(used by `vec![val; n]` for non-primitive `Clone` elements), `Vec::clone`, and
non-`TrivialClone` `slice::to_vec` / `slice::to_vec_in` normally bypass
`Vec::push` and write directly through `as_mut_ptr()` + `SetLenOnDrop` +
`set_len()` (or read `self.buf.alloc` via `self.allocator()`). Routing those
paths through `Vec::with_capacity` / `reserve` / `push` removes `SetLenOnDrop`
codegen and keeps non-primitive `Vec`s eligible for `NativeVec`, while
preserving the fast `IsZero` (`alloc_zeroed`) and `TrivialClone`
(`copy_to_nonoverlapping` / `append_elements`) specializations for `Vec`s that
remain on `Baseline` (and keeping `in_place_collect.rs` untouched).

